From 9504dffb721a6b63059b6a55ed294a16e8b6efba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 07:56:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 34/36] Implement zwp_primary_selection_device_manager_v1 and
 BTN_MIDDLE

Clone the wl_data_device quartet (OwlDataDevice/Source/Offer bases,
reused as-is) into a primary-selection-only sibling, since the
protocol is wl_data_device minus drag-and-drop. Focus-tracked
selection replay is wired into OwlXdgToplevel and OwlZxdgToplevelV6
the same way the clipboard data device already is.

+[OwlSelection primary] existed but was GNUstep-only; make it
unconditional. On Apple there's no primary-selection pasteboard to
bridge it to, so it stays compositor-internal and only mediates
client-to-client middle-click paste, which needs BTN_MIDDLE
forwarding that OwlSurface never had (only otherMouseDown/Up/Dragged
filtered to buttonNumber 2; other extra buttons have no evdev
mapping and are left unforwarded).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VriRpmuZVKUEyysmR8WdJx
